{
  "_note": "Each kind of foe and the behaviour trees they duel with (crates/core/src/pilot.rs). A tree is checked every 6 ticks on the duel as it was reaction_ticks ago; the first rule whose conditions all hold picks a move, and the move plays until it ends. A rule marked interrupt may break into a move under way, but never into a committed swing. Distances are centimetres, speeds centimetres a second, shares percent. hand_px is how far the pilot moves its mouse a tick, strike_px in a swing. keep_cm is the band a foe keeps to in a duel, that far outside its own reach (pilot::reach, shoulder to tip at full stretch: an orc's cleaver 144 cm, a bandit's short sword 140, the leader's sword 177); beyond_reach and within_reach count from the same reach. An attack steps in to 10 cm inside its reach and steps back out to the band after. The others in a group, all but the one nearest the player, run the ring tree. cuts weighs which cut an attack makes (crates/core/src/swing.rs): level (from the right), backhand (level, from the left), chop, rising, thrust; the pilot makes it as the player does, the left button held and the mouse moved that way once. M7 (wounds, T9): a foe whose sword hand is lost drops its weapon (unarmed); with the other hand whole it can take it up (can_take_up, weapon_within) and fights on with it, weaker. Orcs take theirs up when near and otherwise keep coming; bandits run; the leader goes back for its sword and switches hands.",
